In honor of Bill S. and Casca's prose,
Decline to rhyme, but verse may or not be.

In apoplectic tone I do scry:

> A certain something I have for you
> That wil melt you down to hobbit stew.

Well said!  We'll see!  We'll burn the dusted 'E'
A snack, to bash and tin and souvenier!

> Find some sense and fear my might;
> I'll suck the blood from you tonight.

I fear thee not, good sir Impaling Vlad!
Your kin and ken, both as and as not mere.
My silver wand shall be thine final doom!

> So silly of you to come so near;
> You'll be my next meal, I fear.

Hello, hello, my purple worm-ish friend!
My taste and diet ring, dislikes thee?

> Do you dare to read me cursed?
> Though thick-skulled; you'll still feel worse.

Thine earthly runes, non-blessed as well I see!
Perhaps, perchance, just one is all I need?

> Pardon me, sir, but I think you should
> Stop constantly kicking at that wood.

Good Sir Watch, I'll be on my peaceful way.
Oops!  My black battle blade doth drink thine soul!

> Are you daft, or are you blind?
> Know that you'll soon be out of your mind.

Mister (master) mind flayer, I presume?
My tinning kit would like a word with you.

> Won't you come closer, my dear?
> Let me kill you, with a touch, right here.

Oh no! Your deathly touch!  Work it did not.
It is this dingy magic piece of cloth.
This grey-ish dragon's hide as well it does,
Prevents and saves against this grisley fate.

> I may be blind, but I still can be
> Quite a blast if you hit me.

A sphere! A sphere! My dungeon for a sphere!
What must do I or not to kill safely?

> Watch your step! You might meet your end
> If your hand is your avian friend.

I love the rubber chicken in my pack.
Step and wield and hit and unwield!
Historic statuary shall we make?

> I welcome you in
> To my homely place;
> Though you'll soon be floating
> Upon your face.

Now, now, it's rather dull and dark and grim.
Shall I dig and squeltch and smack then heal up?
Or apply a tooled horn to scare and wake?
